      "chapter_path": "example-cases/samplewiki/companions/proximal-bouncy-particle.html",
      "title": "Literal PBPS reflected Gibbs law and C1 compact mean",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
        "edition": "PBPS arXiv2609.06905v1; pinned Mathlib; Lean4.33.0",
        "anchor": "Fixed PBPS arXiv2609.06905v1 C.1 A3.Ex1 physical4581-4587, A3.Ex2 physical4589-4595, normalized-density differentiation A3.E1 physical4597-4604; authored literal Gaussian posterior-reflection background toward B.13 physical3779-3786.",
        "wording_status": "faithful paraphrase",
        "attribution": "ASTIS-authored source-specific analytic integration for Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang’s C.1 reflected density and normalized mean. Lower-only curvature/all-positive η/compact C1/finite Hilbert/rank0 are explicit sufficient-background generalizations; Tests retain original two-sided curvature/cap/smooth compact source setting. Actual Tf closed-gradient and full rough B.13 are excluded."
      },
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, α>0, and D²V(x)[v,v]≥α‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and let f:E→ℝ be C1 with compact support. Define μ=volume.tilted(−V), R_y=μ.tilted(x↦−‖x−y‖²/(2η)), and the literal source law S_y=volume.tilted(u↦−V((y+u)/2)−‖y−u‖²/(8η)). Then for EVERY y, S_y=(x↦2x−y)_#R_y, and the exact mean function y↦∫f(u)S_y(du) is C1. All actual Gibbs normalization, integrability, affine law and mean regularity ingredients are produced internally. This is attributed analytic integration for PBPS C.1, with explicitly broader sufficient background assumptions, not a standalone printed main theorem or rough B.13.",
      "assumptions": [
        "Finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel E, with canonical volume; rank zero is an explicit authored extension.",
        "C2 potential V, positive α and global Hessian lower bound D²V(x)[v,v]≥α‖v‖²; any η>0; signed compact C1 real f.",
        "The paper consumer retains the original upper Hessian β, βη≤1 and smooth compact f. Their omission here is explicitly sufficient-background generalization, never a repair of the source main statement.",
        "μ, R_y and S_y are the exact normalized tilts displayed at every y. No caller probability, L1, partition, Jacobian, affine law, derivative or domain certificate is assumed."
      ],
      "formulae": [
        {
          "label": "Literal PBPS reflected Gibbs law and C1 compact mean",
          "tex": "\\mu(dx)=Z_V^{-1}e^{-V(x)}dx,\\quad R_y(dx)=Z_R(y)^{-1}e^{-V(x)-\\|x-y\\|^2/(2\\eta)}dx,\\quad S_y(du)=Z_S(y)^{-1}e^{-V((y+u)/2)-\\|y-u\\|^2/(8\\eta)}du,\\quad S_y=(2x-y)_\\#R_y\\ (\\forall y),\\quad m(y)=\\int f\\,dS_y\\in C^1."
        }
      ],
      "obligations": [
